  "id": "preformism",
  "term": "preformism",
  "definition": "Preformism is a theory of development holding that the adult organism is already represented in the germ, so development is mainly the unfolding, sorting, and growth of what is already there rather than the creation of genuinely new parts. In its older form, it claimed the adult parts existed in miniature; in its newer form, it says the germ contains definite material elements or regions corresponding to later body parts.",
